Supplementary Table 3. Associations observed at p<5x10-8 and variant features.	Unnamed: 1	Unnamed: 2	Unnamed: 3	Unnamed: 4	Unnamed: 5	Unnamed: 6	Unnamed: 7	Unnamed: 8	Unnamed: 9	Unnamed: 10	Unnamed: 11	Unnamed: 12	Unnamed: 13	Unnamed: 14	Unnamed: 15	Unnamed: 16	Unnamed: 17	Unnamed: 18	Unnamed: 19	Unnamed: 20	Unnamed: 21	Unnamed: 22
F: Non-coincident variants having 1000G-EUR AF <0.02 and SardiNIA AF at least 2* 1000G-EUR AF																						
Standard statistical tests based on allelic frequency (Population-Branch Statistic - PBS) and  haplotype diversity (integrated Haplotype Score -  iHS, cross-population extended haplotype homozygosity (xp-EHH) and the number of segregating Sites by Length - nSL), have been applied as previously described in Steri et al, NEJM 2017. 																						
Significance of statistical tests was evaluated using percentiles, as in Steri et al, NEJM 2017. For simplicity, percentiles >99-th are highlighted in green and >95-th in yellow.																						
Variants were defined under positive selection if at least two independent tests on the haplotype diversity showed values in the 95th percentile of the statistic distribution. 																						
12 variants were not evaluated for positive selection because of low frequency in the datasets we used for the analyses.																						
																						
